From dd28956f5537bfe32d0d28fc90bf7b39162b8ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:32:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(Detective #120): the container family's dict swap
 and ctype to and from a set are pinned by intent tests

The defect, verbatim. "`dict` is partial. Drop-field (`return_drop`) and default-field
(`return_field_default`) are generated. The key/value swap is not. The catalog's reason: the swap raises
on an unhashable value, so it is not total on dict." and "`ctype` converts no sequence to or from a set.
The catalog's reason: list->set is not total, because elements may be unhashable, and set->list has no
deterministic order."

Why the obvious fix is wrong. Generating the swap for every dict return makes it a crash kill wherever a
value is unhashable, and a swap that quietly returns the dict unchanged there is a built-in survivor. Both
reasons are facts about the VALUES a function returns, which the baseline run observes (38bec04): the swap
is generated at a return site only where it was applied to every dict returned there without raising and
changed one; list or tuple to set only where every element was hashable; set to a sorted list (frozenset to
a sorted tuple) only where the elements were mutually orderable, which is also what makes the order
deterministic (not iteration order, which PYTHONHASHSEED moves).

What each state means. Per site, from the observation: `@L!ok=<mode>` (applies), `@L!no=<mode>=TypeError`
(a value of the right type made the attempt raise: not generated, and the function's `mu_minus_withheld`
names the mode, the line and the exception), `@L!no=<mode>=no_effect_observed` (the swap of an empty dict
is the empty dict: a built-in survivor, so not generated, and named). A value outside the premise that a
mutant meets later comes back unchanged from `perturb_return`, never as a crash.

What was NOT closed. The generation is wired through `run_function_profiling(two_sign=True)` only;
Detective's own harvest still carries type names (see 38bec04), so a Detective `--two-sign` run does not
yet generate the premised operators. An OrderedDict or defaultdict is not offered the swap (exact `dict`
only), and the swap's collapse of equal values is the perturbation, not a defect.

Sensitivity: with the premise bypassed (a mode is "ok" whenever offered) 4 of the 24 intent tests fail.
Pin: the pure decisions are pinned in 38bec04.

Tests: tests/test_mu_minus_container_premise_intent.py 24 passed; with the catalog, doc, policy and
instrumentation-ownership guards 95 passed under Python 3.14 and 95 under 3.12, PYTHONUNBUFFERED unset.
ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
